    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2023.03.003",
      "sequence": 10,
      "source_sequence": 11,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Reprint of: On the network topology of variance decompositions: Measuring the connectedness of financial firms",
      "title_cn": "重印：关于方差分解的网络拓扑结构：衡量金融机构的关联性",
      "authors": [
        "Francis X. Diebold",
        "Kamil Yılmaz"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We propose several connectedness measures built from pieces of variance decompositions, and we argue that they provide natural and insightful measures of connectedness. We also show that variance decompositions define weighted, directed networks, so that our connectedness measures are intimately related to key measures of connectedness used in the network literature. Building on these insights, we track daily time-varying connectedness of major U.S. financial institutions’ stock return volatilities in recent years, with emphasis on the financial crisis of 2007–2008.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们提出了若干基于方差分解各部分的关联性度量，并认为它们提供了自然且有洞察力的关联性度量。我们还表明，方差分解定义了加权有向网络，因此我们的关联性度量与网络文献中使用的关键关联性度量密切相关。基于这些见解，我们追踪了近年来美国主要金融机构股票收益波动率的每日时变关联性，重点关注2007-2008的金融危机。",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jeconom.2023.03.003",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-econometrics/vol/234/suppl/C",
      "publication_date": "March 2023",
